course: dictionary
lesson: 246
title: Aloud: heard, not silent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aloud is an adverb. It tells you how something is done: in a voice that other people can hear. «Reading your work aloud helps you hear missing words, clumsy sentences and tense slips.» Here aloud means you say the words so that you can hear them.
explain: Aloud is the opposite of silently. If you read silently, you read in your head and no sound comes out. «Leo read the paper aloud to Grandad every morning» means Grandad could hear every word.
explain: You can also think aloud. This means saying your thoughts as you have them, so others can follow how you work something out. In maths, teachers often ask pupils to think aloud when they solve a problem.
fact: Aloud means in a voice that other people can hear.
fact: Read aloud means reading so that others can hear you.
fact: «Think aloud» means saying your thoughts as you think them.
fact: «Kipling wrote the Just So Stories to be read aloud, so the words are made to be heard.»
exercise: «Reading your work aloud helps you hear missing words.» What does aloud mean here? | *In a voice other people can hear | Very quickly, with no pauses | Silently, inside your head | Written down in pencil
exercise: «Leo read the paper aloud to Grandad every morning.» Find and copy the word that means in a voice others can hear. | *aloud | Grandad | paper | Leo
exercise: The teacher asks Nadia to think aloud. What does she do? | She keeps every thought hidden inside her head | She sings the answer to the class | She writes her answer and hands it in without a word | *She says her thoughts out loud as she works
test: Ella wondered aloud why the moon looked so big. What does wondered aloud mean? | *Said her wonder so others could hear | Forgot the question completely | Drew a picture of the moon | Thought it quietly, without saying anything
test: Which word is the opposite of aloud? | Happily | Loudly | *Silently | Carefully
exam: Mia laughed aloud at the funny joke. What does aloud tell you about her laugh? | *Others could hear it | It was a laugh in a song | It was not a real laugh at all | It was a quiet laugh inside her head
